check for whether the target value is within the entire range.  From the ro=
ot, two branches extend. The left branch leads to node '2' with the conditi=
on '-=E2=88=9E&lt;2&lt;5', and the right branch leads to node '7' with the =
condition '5&lt;7&lt;+=E2=88=9E'.  Each node represents a comparison;  gree=
n dashed arrows indicate a 'True' outcome (the condition is met), and red d=
ashed arrows indicate a 'False' outcome.  Nodes '1' ('-=E2=88=9E&lt;1&lt;2'=
) and '6' ('2&lt;6|5', labeled 'invalid') are children of node '2', while n=
odes '7' ('5&lt;7|7', labeled 'invalid') and '9' ('7&lt;9&lt;+=E2=88=9E') a=
re children of node '7.  The 'invalid' labels suggest that the algorithm ha=
ndles these conditions as errors or out-of-range values.  The final red das=
hed arrow from node '5' points to the text 'return False', indicating that =
if neither the left nor right branch yields a 'True' result, the algorithm =
returns 'False', signifying that the target value was not found within the =
defined ranges." loading=3D"lazy" width=3D"335" height=3D"238" decoding=3D"=
